# Normalize line endings — LF in the repo regardless of the checkout platform.
#
# Verified safe for this repository: no tracked file contains CRLF, and nothing
# here is byte-compared. The CRLF behaviour cfgkit does test — that a list
# element's trailing carriage return is trimmed — is asserted with Go string
# literals in edge_cases_test.go, not with an on-disk fixture, so normalization
# cannot weaken it.
#
# A repo that DID hold byte-exact fixtures would need to exempt them here,
# because `text=auto` would rewrite them on checkout and the assertions would
# then pass or fail depending on the developer's OS.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated — collapse in diffs and keep out of language statistics.
go.sum linguist-generated=true
go.work.sum linguist-generated=true

# Documentation is the majority of the byte count in some adapter modules and
# would otherwise make GitHub report this as a Markdown project.
*.md linguist-documentation=true

# No rules for images, PDFs or vendor/: this repository contains none, ships no
# branding assets by decision, and vendors nothing. A rule describing files that
# do not exist is a rule nobody can verify.
